<title>USA: Landry's sees 106 to 108 units by year-end.</title>
<headline>Landry's sees 106 to 108 units by year-end.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Landry's Seafood Restaurants Inc on Wednesday said it expected to have 106 to 108 units by the end of 1997, compared with 76 at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;Expansion is ahead of schedule,&quot; Tilman Fertitta, chairman, told a Piper Jaffray investment conference in Minneapolis.</p>
<p>He said Landry's, a casual dining seafood restaurant chain, spends about one to two percent of revenues on marketing.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
